        <tr>
          <td style="text-align: left;"><strong>Date: </strong><i>July 8, 2019 at 4:18:33 PM PDT</i></td>
          <td style="text-align: right;"><strong>Observer Location: </strong><i>At Site</i></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td style="text-align: left; padding-bottom: 5px;"><strong>Inferred Origin:</strong><i> Tectonic</i></td>
          <td style="text-align: right; padding-bottom: 5px;"><strong>Inferred Source Event:</strong> <i>M7.1</i></td>
        </tr>
       </table>
       <table>
        <tr>
        	<th>Rupture/Deformation Characteristics</th>
        </tr>
        <tr><td><strong>Overall Fault Strike: </strong><i>161°</i>, <strong>Dip: </strong><i>87°</i></td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>Rupture Width: </strong><i>75 m</i></td></tr>
        <tr><td style="padding-bottom: 5px;">
       <dl>
        <dt><u>Description</u></dt>
        <dd style="padding-bottom: 5px;"><i>Rupture cuts road. Wide zone of distributed faulting, maybe 30 m wide in upthrown block (more localized close to fault), another 40 m in downthrown block (wider zone of cracks), 75 m total. Right lateral displacement of 296 +/- 20 cm. A10-R1 waypoint on Chris's GPS. Devon walking northern margin of offset road, fault trace, and doing some profiles across. Down to west faulting. Vertical measured by sighting in with brunton, vertical offset of 3.44 m +/- 20 cm total. S/D = 161/87. Graben in downthrown block. May coincide with a pre-existing scarp?</i></dd>
       </dl>
      </td></tr>
       </table>
       <table>
        <tr>
        	<th>Slip/Separation Measurements</th>
        </tr>
        <tr><td><strong>Observed Feature: </strong><i>Road</i></td></tr>
        <tr><td>
          <dl>  
         	 <dt><strong><u>Horizontal Separation</u></strong></dt>
        	   <dd>
        	   <strong>Length: </strong><i>296 ± 20 cm right-lateral</i><br/>
            </dt>
           </dl>
         </td></tr>
        <tr><td style="padding-bottom: 5px;"><strong>Vertical Separation: </strong><i>344 ± 20 cm west side down</i></td></tr>
       </table>
       <table>
        <tr>
        	<td></td>
        </tr>
       </table>
