  <Placemark>
    <name>60 ± 10 cm left-lateral</name>
    <Snippet maxLines="0"></Snippet>
    <description>
    	<![CDATA[
       <table>
        <tr style="background-color:#ccd7e5; border-bottom: 1px solid;">
          <td style="text-align: left; font-weight: bold;">Station ID: 30375</td>
          <td style="text-align: right; font-weight: bold;">Observer ID: STOB-004-KSG7</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td style="text-align: left;"><strong>Principal Observer: </strong><i>K. Scharer/USGS</i></td>
          <td style="text-align: right;">
          <div style="color:blue;" class="popup" onclick="myFunction()"><u><strong>Field Team: </strong><i>07/09-5</i></u>
           <span class="popuptext" id="myPopup"><p align="center"><b><u>Team Members</u></b><br/>J. Delano/USGS<br/>N. Graehl/CGS<br/>K. Kendrick/USGS<br/>B. Olson/CGS<br/>B. Philibosian/USGS</p></span>
          </div>
          </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td style="text-align: left;"><strong>Date: </strong><i>July 9, 2019</i></td>
          <td style="text-align: right;"><strong>Observer Location: </strong><i>Other</i></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td style="text-align: left; padding-bottom: 5px;"><strong>Inferred Origin:</strong><i> Tectonic</i></td>
          <td style="text-align: right; padding-bottom: 5px;"><strong>Inferred Source Event:</strong> <i>M6.4</i></td>
        </tr>
       </table>
       <table>
        <tr>
        	<th>Rupture/Deformation Characteristics</th>
        </tr>
        <tr><td><strong>Overall Fault Strike: </strong><i>55° ± 2°</i></td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>Rupture Width: </strong><i>15 m</i></td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>Fault Expression: </strong><i>Zone of deformation</i></td></tr>
        <tr><td style="padding-bottom: 5px;">
       <dl>
        <dt><u>Description</u></dt>
        <dd style="padding-bottom: 5px;"><i>Offset of fence poles obliquely oriented to 15 m wide wide fault zone where fault bends to more easterly orientation. Measurements made across 2.7 m wide aperture of main fault. Trends of poles were fit visually to poles outside of fault zone and measured on several fault orientations (53-57 degrees).  While the southern poles bend to left (west) near fault, the northern poles show no clear bend (and could be argued to bend to west as well, opposite to expectations).  Range in offsets is 57-61 cm, at least 10 cm uncertainty. </i></dd>
       </dl>
      </td></tr>
       </table>
       <table>
        <tr>
