       <table>
        <tr>
        	<th>Rupture/Deformation Characteristics</th>
        </tr>
        <tr><td><strong>Overall Fault Strike: </strong><i>152°</i></td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>Rupture Width: </strong><i>8.4 m</i></td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>Fault Expression: </strong><i>Zone of deformation</i></td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>Scarp Facing Direction: </strong><i>West</i></td></tr>
        <tr><td style="padding-bottom: 5px;">
       <dl>
        <dt><u>Description</u></dt>
        <dd style="padding-bottom: 5px;"><i>Two parallel tire tracks cross multi-stranded fault zone.  Offset (if any) on the easternmost strand was not surveyed on the northern tire track, so the southern tire track is reported.  Full fault zone width is 8.4 m, but no change in tire trend within fault zone so narrower aperture (1.9 m) is used to estimate range.  Horizontal uncertainty is 20 cm, equivalent to variability measured at different locations and the tire width. </i></dd>
       </dl>
      </td></tr>
       </table>
