          <div style="color:blue;" class="popup" onclick="myFunction()"><u><strong>Field Team: </strong><i>07/10-5</i></u>
           <span class="popuptext" id="myPopup"><p align="center"><b><u>Team Members</u></b><br/>S. Angster/USGS<br/>T. Dawson/CGS<br/>C. DuRoss/USGS<br/>B. Olson/CGS<br/>K. Scharer/USGS</p></span>
          </div>
          </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td style="text-align: left;"><strong>Date: </strong><i>July 10, 2019</i></td>
          <td style="text-align: right;"><strong>Observer Location: </strong><i>Other</i></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td style="text-align: left; padding-bottom: 5px;"><strong>Inferred Origin:</strong><i> Tectonic</i></td>
          <td style="text-align: right; padding-bottom: 5px;"><strong>Inferred Source Event:</strong> <i>M7.1</i></td>
        </tr>
       </table>
       <table>
        <tr>
        	<th>Rupture/Deformation Characteristics</th>
        </tr>
        <tr><td><strong>Overall Fault Strike: </strong><i>146°</i></td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>Rupture Width: </strong><i>9 m</i></td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>Fault Expression: </strong><i>Zone of deformation</i></td></tr>
        <tr><td style="padding-bottom: 5px;">
       <dl>
        <dt><u>Description</u></dt>
        <dd style="padding-bottom: 5px;"><i>Offset of tire track. Western track curves to south as it approaches fault zone, trend changes from 82 to 87 degrees. The latter is closer in orientation to the eastern tire track (91 degrees). Eastern track also more southerly in fault zone, suggesting rotation. Either tracks bent at (eventual) fault or more proximal value a better estimate. Main fault expressed with large variability in fault zone width along strike.  The recorded aperture (6.3 m) is the distance from the bend in the western track to last survey point of eastern track (which is west of eastern strand).  Discrete measurements of 12 cm on eastern strand, 382 cm across main fault sum to 403 cm.  The wider aperture offset is 442 cm.  Recorded values reflect this uncertainty.  Vertical separation is 47 cm at main fault zone, recorded uncertainty reflects variation in far field elevations (15 cm).</i></dd>
       </dl>
      </td></tr>
       </table>
       <table>
        <tr>
        	<th>Slip/Separation Measurements</th>
        </tr>
        <tr><td><strong>Observed Feature: </strong><i>Tire track</i></td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>Measurement Aperture: </strong><i>6.3 m</i></td></tr>
        <tr><td>
          <dl>  
         	 <dt><strong><u>Slip Vector</u></strong></dt>
        	   <dd>
              <strong>Azimuth: </strong><i>146°</i></dd>
            </dt>
           </dl>
         </td></tr>
        <tr><td>
          <dl>  
         	 <dt><strong><u>Horizontal Offset</u></strong></dt>
        	   <dd>
        	   <strong>Length: </strong><i>422 ± 20 cm right-lateral</i><br/>
              <strong>Azimuth: </strong><i>146°</i></dd>
            </dt>
           </dl>
         </td></tr>
        <tr><td style="padding-bottom: 5px;"><strong>Vertical Offset: </strong><i>47 ± 15 cm west side down</i></td></tr>
       </table>
       <table>
        <tr>
        	<td></td>
        </tr>
       </table>
