        	<th>Rupture/Deformation Characteristics</th>
        </tr>
        <tr><td><strong>Overall Fault Strike: </strong><i>327° – 355°</i></td></tr>
        <tr><td style="padding-bottom: 5px;">
       <dl>
        <dt><u>Description</u></dt>
        <dd style="padding-bottom: 5px;"><i>Summary (with additional measurements) for all offsets on this roadway: Northeasternmost trace fault bearing N5W.  Slip vector direction N55W. 3.5 cm 3 cm extension 2 deg plunge.  Next trace to SW 4 cm slip 8 mm vertical down to south 37 west bearing.  Next trace to SW 82 cm 38 W bearing.  Next trace to SW 1.48-1.49 m N17W. Too much deformation to estimate vertical. Adjacent less 55 cm.  Next trace to SW 12 cm N31W. Vertical is difficult due to deformation.  Next trace to SW 4 cm N29W.  Next trace to SW double yellow 14 cm 13.5 cm N33W.  About 5 ft vertical on principal trace  - 2.675 m total slip    </i></dd>
       </dl>
      </td></tr>
       </table>
       <table>
        <tr>
        	<th>Slip/Separation Measurements</th>
        </tr>
        <tr><td><strong>Observed Feature: </strong><i>Road</i></td></tr>
