        <tr><td style="padding-bottom: 5px;">
       <dl>
        <dt><u>Description</u></dt>
        <dd style="padding-bottom: 5px;"><i>Faulting. Orientation 165°
From R. Zinke: Measurements: Fault Parallel: minimum 1.5 cm, preferred 2 cm, maximum 2.5 cm.  Fault Perpendicular: minimum 3 cm, preferred 4 cm, maximum 5 cm.  Vertical: minimum 2.5 cm, preferred 3 cm, maximum 4.5 cm.  Fault strand is well-defined here, then becomes very thin, characterized by subtle cracking to the south.  Intermittent (discontinuous) cracking observed for 100 + m south or southeast from point 435. </i></dd>
       </dl>
      </td></tr>
       </table>
       <table>
        <tr>
