          </div>
          </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td style="text-align: left;"><strong>Date: </strong><i>July 24, 2019</i></td>
          <td style="text-align: right;"><strong>Observer Location: </strong><i>Other</i></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td style="text-align: left; padding-bottom: 5px;"><strong>Inferred Origin:</strong><i> Tectonic</i></td>
          <td style="text-align: right; padding-bottom: 5px;"><strong>Inferred Source Event:</strong> <i>M7.1</i></td>
        </tr>
       </table>
       <table>
        <tr>
        	<th>Rupture/Deformation Characteristics</th>
        </tr>
        <tr><td><strong>Overall Fault Strike: </strong><i>134°</i></td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>Rupture Width: </strong><i>9 m</i></td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>Fault Expression: </strong><i>Scarp</i></td></tr>
        <tr><td style="padding-bottom: 5px;">
       <dl>
        <dt><u>Description</u></dt>
        <dd style="padding-bottom: 5px;"><i>Offset of narrow gully in steep terrain.  Fault appears single stranded though recorded width includes wider zone shown by fault strands to NW and SE (9 m).  Gully measured across a 3 m aperture that includes right bend in western gully-unknown if this was pre-existing.  Range in measurements is 283-498 cm; uncertainty of 30 cm subtracted from lower value, upper value assumed to be maximum.  Reported mean (uncertainty) is thus 375 cm (123).  </i></dd>
       </dl>
      </td></tr>
       </table>
       <table>
        <tr>
        	<th>Slip/Separation Measurements</th>
        </tr>
        <tr><td><strong>Observed Feature: </strong><i>Gully</i></td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>Measurement Aperture: </strong><i>3 m</i></td></tr>
        <tr><td>
          <dl>  
