        <tr>
          <td style="text-align: left; padding-bottom: 5px;"><strong>Inferred Origin:</strong><i> Tectonic</i></td>
          <td style="text-align: right; padding-bottom: 5px;"><strong>Inferred Source Event:</strong> <i>M7.1</i></td>
        </tr>
       </table>
       <table>
        <tr>
        	<th>Rupture/Deformation Characteristics</th>
        </tr>
        <tr><td><strong>Overall Fault Strike: </strong><i>137°</i></td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>Rupture Width: </strong><i>3.8 m</i></td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>Fault Expression: </strong><i>Zone of deformation</i></td></tr>
        <tr><td style="padding-bottom: 5px;">
       <dl>
        <dt><u>Description</u></dt>
        <dd style="padding-bottom: 5px;"><i>Offset of narrow gully across two discrete faults 3.8 m apart.  Western gully has right bend about 2 m west of surveyed fault zone (uphill direction), so measurement aperture (5.5 m) includes this as possible result of faulting. Discrete gully end-to-end offset of eastern fault trace (40 cm) and western trace (185 cm) provides minimum of 225 m. Offset across the wider aperture of 312 cm, with 30 cm uncertainties based on channel bottom width preferred given variability in fault trace and uphill bend of gully. </i></dd>
       </dl>
      </td></tr>
       </table>
       <table>
        <tr>
        	<th>Slip/Separation Measurements</th>
        </tr>
        <tr><td><strong>Observed Feature: </strong><i>Gully</i></td></tr>
