  <Placemark>
    <name>508 ± 100 cm right-lateral</name>
    <Snippet maxLines="0"></Snippet>
    <description>
    	<![CDATA[
       <table>
        <tr style="background-color:#ccd7e5; border-bottom: 1px solid;">
          <td style="text-align: left; font-weight: bold;">Station ID: 30374</td>
          <td style="text-align: right; font-weight: bold;">Observer ID: KSG7-11</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td style="text-align: left;"><strong>Principal Observer: </strong><i>K. Scharer/USGS</i></td>
          <td style="text-align: right;">
          <div style="color:blue;" class="popup" onclick="myFunction()"><u><strong>Field Team: </strong><i>07/24-1</i></u>
           <span class="popuptext" id="myPopup"><p align="center"><b><u>Team Members</u></b><br/>S. Bennett/USGS<br/>B. Philibosian/USGS<br/>K. Scharer/USGS<br/>G. Seitz/CGS</p></span>
          </div>
          </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td style="text-align: left;"><strong>Date: </strong><i>July 24, 2019</i></td>
          <td style="text-align: right;"><strong>Observer Location: </strong><i>At Site</i></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td style="text-align: left; padding-bottom: 5px;"><strong>Inferred Origin:</strong><i> Tectonic</i></td>
          <td style="text-align: right; padding-bottom: 5px;"><strong>Inferred Source Event:</strong> <i>M7.1</i></td>
        </tr>
       </table>
       <table>
        <tr>
        	<th>Rupture/Deformation Characteristics</th>
        </tr>
        <tr><td><strong>Overall Fault Strike: </strong><i>142°</i></td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>Rupture Width: </strong><i>3.7 m</i></td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>Fault Expression: </strong><i>Zone of deformation</i></td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>Scarp Facing Direction: </strong><i>West</i></td></tr>
        <tr><td style="padding-bottom: 5px;">
       <dl>
        <dt><u>Description</u></dt>
        <dd style="padding-bottom: 5px;"><i>Offset gully on steep western facing bedrock slope.  Gully is ~fault normal east of scarp, trends westerly just west of scarp and then bends more southerly (fault normal) about 2 m west of its termination (wider aperture is 3.7 m, narrower aperture is 1.7 m).  Range is 406 to 611 cm; wider offset may be older event, if gully bend was pre-existing.  Worth comparing these values with field measurements by Bennett and Seitz.</i></dd>
       </dl>
      </td></tr>
       </table>
       <table>
        <tr>
        	<th>Slip/Separation Measurements</th>
        </tr>
        <tr><td><strong>Observed Feature: </strong><i>Gully</i></td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>Measurement Aperture: </strong><i>1.7 – 3.7 m</i></td></tr>
        <tr><td>
